   "text": "This is a bicyclic peptide on a tris(thiomethyl)benzene core, with a DOTA chelator on the N-terminus and a C-terminal primary amide. I read it region by region.\n\n**Sequence, from the DOTA end:** DOTA\u2013Cys\u2013Ala\u2013Asn\u2013Glu\u20131Nal\u2013Ala\u2013Cys\u2013Glu\u2013Asp\u2013Phe\u2013Tyr\u2013Asp\u2013tert-leucine\u2013Cys\u2013NH2.\n\n- **DOTA:** a 12-membered ring with four nitrogens and three free CH2CO2H arms. The fourth arm is a CH2C(=O) amide to the N-terminal Cys.\n- **Scaffold:** a benzene ring with CH2 groups at positions 1, 3 and 5. Each CH2 is bonded to the sulfur of one of the three Cys residues, so the three thioether links form two peptide loops.\n- **Side chains:** Glu is CH2CH2CO2H, Asp is CH2CO2H, Asn is CH2C(=O)NH2, and Phe is benzyl. Tyr is 4-hydroxybenzyl, and 1Nal is naphthalen-1-ylmethyl. The Ala residues carry a methyl, and the tert-leucine carries a tert-butyl.\n- **Stereochemistry:** I assigned every \u03b1-carbon as the natural L configuration, which is how the wedges and hashes read, rather than checking each one individually.\n\nIn the SMILES, ring closure %11 joins the Cys2 CH2 to its scaffold CH2\u2013S, and %12 does the same for Cys3.\n\nSMILES: OC(=O)CN1CCN(CC(=O)O)CCN(CC(=O)O)CCN(CC1)CC(=O)N[C@@H](CSCc1cc(CS%11)cc(CS%12)c1)C(=O)N[C@@H](C)C(=O)N[C@@H](CC(N)=O)C(=O)N[C@@H](CCC(=O)O)C(=O)N[C@@H](Cc2cccc3ccccc23)C(=O)N[C@@H](C)C(=O)N[C@@H](C%11)C(=O)N[C@@H](CCC(=O)O)C(=O)N[C@@H](CC(=O)O)C(=O)N[C@@H](Cc4ccccc4)C(=O)N[C@@H](Cc5ccc(O)cc5)C(=O)N[C@@H](CC(=O)O)C(=O)N[C@@H](C(C)(C)C)C(=O)N[C@@H](C%12)C(N)=O"
  }
